\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  A new year comes, the old has gone
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  To time eternal yonder;
\par  May't give the slow of heart the thought
\par  On passing time to ponder.
\par  This precious time of every year
\par  That good fruit of faith it must bear.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Where is the fruit we could have brought
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  And in the past were bearing?
\par  Alas! In vain our God has sought,
\par  The lack of fruit despairing.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  What shame when we before God stand,
\par  No fruit, but only leaves in hand.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  "Cut down the tree, it gives no fruit",
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Commands the Lord and Master;
\par  "It takes from others room to root,
\par  Without room, death comes faster.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Cut off the root, take axe in hand
\par For without fruit no tree may stand!"
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. The Gard'ner pleads: "Do not uproot,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj But save the tree from dying!
\par With care it still may bring much fruit,
\par Our patience justifying.
\par With-hold Thy judgement, Lord, this year ;
\par Let sunshine, rain and growth appear.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  Give strength, the will that we may strive
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 To walk in faith before Thee;
\par Sustained in love, we will survive
\par To honour and adore Thee.
\par Pour out Thy grace upon Thine own;
\par Thy holy will to us make known.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

